				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Attention Fellow Adventurers:
<br />

<br />
Fusion has decided it is time to press forward in our guild advancement.  This means that we have been attempting to do more high level raids and advancement raids, as well as back flagging our newer recruits and other alternate raids as "practice" raids.
<br />

<br />
A lot of other guild's members have shown an interest in participating in our raids and realizing the potential good that could come of it, Fusion has decided to change its raiding policies.
<br />

<br />
What does this mean to your guild?
<br />

<br />
Fusion will be practicing an "Open Door" policy, meaning, if we're raiding and we have space, we will allow ANY member level 60 or above, of any ANTI-PK guild to join our raid if space is available, on a first come first served basis.
<br />

<br />
This of course means that there could be circumstances where two anti, but warring guilds, have to work side-by-side.  We expect that NO guild war should interrupt an event that benefits EVERYONE as equally as possible.  That means, MiM could be fighting side-by-side DoZ, Eximos with Shaded Militia, etc.  Warring, "shit talk", or any other activity will not be tolerated and any parties practicing such actions will be ejected from the raids and will be excluded from future raids.
<br />

<br />
However, this "Open Door" policy isn't going to be a free ride, Fusion will likewise expect a "quid pro quo" from participating guilds.  Should a participating guild be raiding a flagging, or some sort of progression event PoP, VT related, GoD or otherwise, and there is space available in the participating guild's raid, Fusion would appreciate being allowed to participate.
<br />

<br />
It's long been known that Fusion has been a guild where certain other guilds direct their unflagged recruits to go to get their lower tier flags and such, and looking at the long and short of it, that's fine, as long as those that have decided to stay with Fusion have the opportunity to get the experience neccessary in the upper tier flag events to gain the knowledge to run our own events and, again, practicing the "open door" policy allow all qualifying anti's to join.
<br />

<br />
We appreciate your attention and consideration of this matter.
<br />

<br />
If you'd like to discuss specifics of this, please feel free to visit the Fusion web site at http:\\fusion.eliteguildz.com.
<br />

<br />
Fusion Council<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Dimento Graven</div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
